body: "## Reproduced defect (unreleased PR #2)\n\nTested **20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b**, package 2026.10.18, Node 24.19.0, pinned @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.18. This concerns the implementation in [PR #2](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/pull/2), not the scaffold currently on main.\n\nA typed model failure in an already-created child is converted into a parent tool refusal. The parent can then finish successfully, but the persisted call graph contains an unfinished child. Replay rejects that successfully completed run, and resume returns the root answer without repairing or retrying the child.\n\n## Source goal\n\nThe [canonical epic](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/.agents/pm/epics/pm-rlm-a1ih.toon) requires durable budgets, crash resume and replay. The [README](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/README.md) promises replay of the recorded actions with a byte-identical answer and recoverable tool refusals.\n\n## Sanitized reproduction\n\nUse a temporary SDK tracker and deterministic model only; no provider, network inference, credentials or existing tracker data are needed. At the tested checkout, save this as a temporary test at the repository root and execute `node --test review-repro.test.ts` (remove it before repository-wide lint):\n\n```ts\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { test } from 'node:test';\nimport { tracker, ScriptedModel } from './test/helpers.ts';\nimport { runRlm, replayRlm, resumeRlm, treeRlm } from './src/engine.ts';\nimport { RlmError } from './src/errors.ts';\nimport { PROTOCOL } from './src/protocol.ts';\n\ntest('failed child leaves a successful run unreplayable', async t => {\n  const { workspace } = await tracker(t);\n  const model = new ScriptedModel(request => {\n    const input = JSON.parse(request.prompt.slice(PROTOCOL.length + 1));\n    if (input.depth === 1) throw new RlmError('model', 'Transient offline model');\n    return JSON.stringify(input.transcript.length\n      ? { action: 'finish', answer: 'recovered' }\n      : { action: 'spawn', subgoal: 'child',\n          slice: { fragments: [], estimated_tokens: 2 } });\n  });\n  const result = await runRlm('root', { workspace, model });\n  assert.equal(result.answer, 'recovered');\n  await assert.rejects(replayRlm(workspace, result.run), {\n    code: 'replay', message: 'Recorded call graph has unreachable calls'\n  });\n  assert.equal((await resumeRlm(workspace, result.run, model)).answer, 'recovered');\n  const tree = await treeRlm(workspace, result.run);\n  assert.deepEqual(tree.calls.map(call => call.status), ['closed', 'in_progress']);\n});\n```\n\nObserved: the regression test passes, proving the undesirable behavior. The successful run reports 2 calls; the root is closed and the child remains in progress even after resume. The same observation was repeated with telemetry disabled and isolated HOME.\n\n## Cause and impact\n\n- [spawn](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/src/engine.ts#L73-L81) persists the child before executing it\n- [execute's catch](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/20521faad22bb54536b90c8e86960a5a9093747b/src/engine.ts#L121-L126) catches any nested RlmError and stores only `{refused: code}`\n- Replay skips refused steps, then rejects the unvisited child; resume sees the completed root and returns without resuming that child\n\nA transient endpoint error during recursion therefore breaks replay/recovery guarantees even when the top-level command reports success. This is distinct from the existing oversized-read/context-limit review: an empty child slice and ordinary typed transport failure suffice.\n\n## Expected behavior / regression criteria\n\nDefine a durable outcome for materialized children when their spawn fails. Either propagate an interrupted child as a resumable run failure, or record a terminal failed child and replay that refusal consistently. A root reported as successful must remain replayable, and resume must not report recovery while silently leaving an orphaned in-progress child. Add coverage for child transport failure and context refusal after child creation, preserving reservation accounting and existing SIGKILL/digest-reuse behavior.\n\n## Scope and deduplication\n\nReviewed all-status issues/PRs (#1–3), PR #2's 10 existing inline comments/review, and the eight canonical tracker records at this commit. No matching failed-child/replay record was present. This is a deterministic local reproduction; no live-provider quality, Bun acceptance, release readiness or deployed behavior is claimed.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (2)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-19T05:20:07Z)\n>\n> Additional terminal-child evidence on PR #2, exact head `7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba`: a transient SDK read failure during child completion can now be swallowed as a tool refusal, allowing a successful root to leave its completed child `in_progress`.\n> \n> The canonical [ledger feature](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/.agents/pm/features/pm-rlm-6a8t.toon) requires Task evidence and a matching call graph. The PR explicitly promises evidence, closure and claim release for every child in a successfully returned run. The original transport-failure path reported in this issue is repaired; this is a new completion-read regression against the same terminal-child invariant, distinct from the repaired history-read and comment-write cases. Explicit resume does repair this new case, so the older non-recoverability claim does not apply.\n> \n> Cause:\n> - The newly added `sdkRead` around [materialize's complete-list read](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/ledger.ts#L105-L121) converts an unexpected SDK error into `RlmError('incomplete')`\n> - A child finish is already checkpointed when `complete()` invokes that read. [spawn](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/engine.ts#L91-L100) sees `call.result` and rethrows without repairing evidence\n> - The parent's [generic typed-error catch](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/engine.ts#L148-L164) records `{refused:'incomplete'}` and continues. Terminal reconciliation runs [before root execution only](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/7f705e13b11aec9d85109112d868932c675ed3ba/src/engine.ts#L169-L181)\n> \n> Reproduction: a real SDK-created synthetic tracker and scripted parent/child model. Once the child's finish response is produced, a one-shot wrapper around `PmClient.prototype.listAllComplete` creates a directory named `tasks/review-unreadable.toon`, calls the original SDK method, and removes the directory in `finally`. Thus the SDK itself produces a real filesystem-read error; the wrapper supplies neither a fabricated SDK result nor a fabricated exception. All other SDK operations remain real.\n> \n> Actual on this head: `runRlm` returns `answer:'root success', calls:2`. Root item is closed; child has durable `result:'child success'` but remains `in_progress`. Parent's spawn observation is `{refused:'incomplete'}`. Replay already returns the recorded root answer despite the open SDK child. Calling resume explicitly repairs and closes the child without a second child inference. The observed defect is incomplete terminal evidence/closure at successful return, not an unreplayable or permanently stranded run.\n> \n> Control: the identical fault on prior head `cdac605b19b95ac02caed2d96c83f1e9c080f2e6` aborts the root with no root result or parent observation. Resume then repairs the child and finishes with one total child inference. This demonstrates a regression in the new typed-read classification rather than a failure of the test fixture.\n> \n> Expected/regression criteria: completion-reconciliation failures must not be converted into a successful tool refusal while evidence remains unfinished. Either abort and preserve the unfinished parent observation until resume repairs it, or reconcile every terminal child before returning success. Cover transient errors at both reads in completion, then verify actual SDK Task closure/evidence/claim release, replay, and no repeat inference after recovery. Keep malformed source history as a recoverable read refusal and preserve the separate fatal evidence-write regression.\n> \n> Validation limits: fresh typecheck and all 113 unit tests pass; 46 non-install behavioral revert proofs pass. The two packed-install proofs were intentionally not rerun because they install dependencies. Isolated copied source was verified against immutable Git blob identities. No provider calls, credentials, dependency changes, original-checkout modifications, or live integrations were used. The reproduction uses deterministic timing instrumentation at the SDK boundary, not a claim that this transient filesystem condition happened in production.\n> \n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-19T07:02:00Z)\n>\n> Post-merge verification: the completion-read case in [the preceding report](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/issues/4#issuecomment-6260265599) still reproduces on exact main/PR #2 merge commit `90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb`, after this issue was closed.\n> \n> I reran the unchanged real-SDK filesystem-fault reproduction on a separately materialized copy verified against all 104 tracked Git blobs. It returns `answer:'root success', calls:2`; the root is closed, but the child has `result:'child success'` and remains `in_progress`. The parent records `{refused:'incomplete'}`. Replay returns the answer; explicit resume closes the child with one total child inference.\n> \n> The relevant path is unchanged: [completion reads](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb/src/ledger.ts#L105-L130) can become typed refusals through [the parent catch](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb/src/engine.ts#L149-L165), while [terminal reconciliation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/90b99a0952f175d4732a133def5d83935db0bbfb/src/engine.ts#L170-L182) occurs only before execution. This remains the previously reported incomplete terminal-evidence/closure case, not a claim that replay or explicit recovery is broken.\n> \n> Please retain this residual case as open work: either propagate completion failure until resume repairs it, or reconcile terminal children before returning success, with coverage for both completion reads. No provider calls, dependency changes or production data were used.\n>"
